{"text": "# Calder & Finch Outfitters, Inc.\n\n## Minutes of the Regular Meeting of the Board of Directors\n\n**Date:** Tuesday, January 20, 2026, 4:00 p.m.\n**Place:** Company office, 1045 NW Bond Street, 2nd floor, Bend, Oregon, and by video\n\n**Directors present:** Marguerite Calder (Chair), Dr. Anjali Deshpande-Hall, Rev. Curtis Whitehorse, Yuki Tanabe (CFO and Secretary)\n**Absent:** Tobias Finch (CEO), excused\n**Also present:** April Sorensen, Sorensen Lyle LLP, outside counsel\n\n### 1. Call to order\n\nMs. Calder called the meeting to order at 4:04 p.m. and confirmed a quorum under ORS 60.337. The minutes of the November meeting were approved without changes. The meeting followed Robert's Rules informally, as usual.\n\n### 2. CEO leave of absence\n\nThe Chair reported that Tobias began chemotherapy on January 6 for non-Hodgkin lymphoma and expects to be away from day-to-day work for at least four months. He asked that staff be told only that he is on medical leave.\n\n**RESOLVED:** Ms. Tanabe is appointed Acting Chief Executive Officer, effective immediately, with an additional stipend of $4,000 per month. Carried 3-0, Ms. Tanabe abstaining.\n\n### 3. Financial report\n\nMs. Tanabe presented the Q4 results. Revenue was $1.82 million, up 6% on the prior year; the Redmond store again lost money ($41k for the quarter). The line of credit with High Desert Community Bank (loan no. 4410-776-02) stands at $310,000 drawn against a $500,000 limit. The company is in compliance with its covenants.\n\n### 4. Delivery van\n\n**RESOLVED:** The company may buy a used 2023 Ram ProMaster cargo van from Cascade Fleet Sales for $38,450 (VIN 3C6LRVDG5PE518204). It replaces the Sprinter, Oregon plate 482 KVM, which will be sold. Carried unanimously.\n\n### 5. Payroll fraud incident\n\nOn December 11, 2025, a payroll clerk responded to a phishing email. The attacker then signed in to the payroll portal from IP address 203.0.113.57 using the Redmond store manager's account (jreyes.redmond) and redirected the direct deposits of two employees. $14,280 was diverted; $9,100 has been recovered. The loss was reported to Summit Ridge Mutual (claim no. CY-25-00817) and to the Bend police (case 2025-00071934). All portal passwords were reset and MFA is now required.\n\n### 6. Executive session: personnel\n\nMs. Sorensen briefed the Board on the BOLI complaint (no. STEMDP251022-41877) filed by Jesse Reyes, the former Redmond store manager, who alleges he was dismissed in October shortly after telling Tobias he is HIV-positive. Management's position is that Mr. Reyes was dismissed over the cash-handling audit. April recommended settling.\n\n**RESOLVED:** Counsel is authorized to settle the Reyes matter for up to $22,500 plus a neutral reference, on confidential terms. Carried 3-1, Rev. Whitehorse opposed.\n\n### 7. Other business\n\n- Donation of $2,500 to the Three Creeks Trail Alliance approved.\n- Bank signers: Tobias is removed temporarily and Dr. Deshpande-Hall is added as second signer on the operating account ending 3382.\n\n### 8. Adjournment\n\nThe next regular meeting is set for March 17, 2026. The meeting adjourned at 5:35 p.m.\n\n*Submitted by Yuki Tanabe, Secretary. Draft; not yet approved.*", "kind": "Markdown document", "detail": "496 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Directors", "Chair", "Rev", "Whitehorse", "Secretary", "Absent", "Also", "Counsel", "Submitted"], "companies": ["Company", "Acting Chief Executive Officer", "Ram", "Board", "Donation", "Bank"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Place", "Bend", "Redmond"], "health": [], "sensitive": [], "names": []}, "judged": {"candidates": 22, "requests": 2, "failures": 0, "places": ["Place", "Bend", "Redmond"], "labels": {"Directors": "person", "Date": "other", "Place": "place", "Company": "organization", "Chair": "person", "Rev": "person", "Whitehorse": "person", "Secretary": "person", "Absent": "person", "Also": "person", "Rules": "other", "Hodgkin": "other", "Acting Chief Executive Of